{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeSeminormalWeight","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeSeminormalWeight","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeFullTwistProduct"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.scalar_fullTwist_eq_single_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.scalar_fullTwist_eq_single_row","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeSeminormalWeight.lean#L221-L228","doc":"**The falsifiability check.**  Feeding that instance to the general theorem gives\n`q^{n(n−1)}` — which is what `theta_single_row_sq` obtains from the two roots of the Hecke relation,\nwith no Jucys–Murphy input at all.  The two routes agree, so the general statement is constrained by\nan independently-proved case rather than free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.scalar_isJMWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.scalar_isJMWeight","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeSeminormalWeight.lean#L209-L219","doc":"**The hypothesis is satisfied.**  `v = 1` in the one-dimensional representation is a\nJucys–Murphy weight vector for the one-row tableau, with exactly the content eigenvalues. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.rowTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.rowTableau","kind":"def","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeSeminormalWeight.lean#L192-L207","doc":"The one-row tableau of shape `[m+1]`: entry `k` sits in cell `(0, k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.scalar_jmRaw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.scalar_jmRaw","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeSeminormalWeight.lean#L182-L190","doc":"In that representation `Lₖ = q^{2k}` — the JM spectrum of the one-row block, on the nose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.scalarGenerators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.scalarGenerators","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeSeminormalWeight.lean#L168-L180","doc":"The **one-dimensional Hecke representation** `σᵢ ↦ q` — the `+q` root of the Hecke relation,\nthe same branch `KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist` uses for the one-row block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.twist_scalar_eq_theta_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.twist_scalar_eq_theta_sq","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeSeminormalWeight.lean#L140-L160","doc":"**The twist scalar is pinned, not merely permitted.**\n\nIf the full twist acts on a nonzero weight vector by *some* scalar `s`, that scalar **is** `θ_λ²`.\nThis is the bridge to `KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.JucysMurphySpectrum`: its `fullTwistScalar_eq` field\nasserts exactly this equation, and here it is a consequence of the per-element eigenvalues rather\nthan a separate assumption.\n\n`NoZeroSMulDivisors R V` is what turns \"acts the same way on `v`\" into \"is the same scalar\"; it is\nstated as a hypothesis rather than derived so that nothing here depends on `V` being a vector\nspace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwist_smul_eq_theta_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwist_smul_eq_theta_sq","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeSeminormalWeight.lean#L126-L138","doc":"**The general-`λ` twist, from the per-element Jucys–Murphy spectrum.**\n\nIf each `Lₖ` acts on `v` by `q^{2·content of the cell holding k}`, then the full twist acts by\n`θ_λ² = q^{2c(λ)}` — for every partition, and independently of which tableau `e` is.\n\nThe remaining assumption is `IsJMWeight` with the content eigenvalues.  That is the seminormal-form\ntheorem and it is **not** proved here; what is no longer assumed is the passage from the individual\neigenvalues to the twist. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.prod_jmEigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.prod_jmEigen","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeSeminormalWeight.lean#L105-L124","doc":"The eigenvalues multiply to `θ_λ²`, for **every** tableau — the same tableau-independence\n`sum_content_of_equiv` supplies, transported through `prod_zpow_eq_zpow_sum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmEigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmEigen","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeSeminormalWeight.lean#L100-L103","doc":"The JM eigenvalue function attached to a tableau: `k ↦ q^{2·content}` of the cell holding `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.entryIdx_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.entryIdx_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeSeminormalWeight.lean#L97-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.entryIdx_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.entryIdx_val","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeSeminormalWeight.lean#L94-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.entryIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.entryIdx","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeSeminormalWeight.lean#L90-L92","doc":"Entry `k` of a tableau on `m+1` cells, as an index.  The `% (m+1)` is a totality device only:\nevery use is at `k < m+1`, where `entryIdx_of_lt` says it is the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwist_smul_of_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwist_smul_of_weight","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeSeminormalWeight.lean#L78-L86","doc":"**The full twist acts on a JM weight vector by the product of its eigenvalues.**\n\n`Δ² = (delta m)^{m+1}` by `jmProd_eq_delta_pow`, so the composite statement the old class assumed is\nnow a consequence of the per-element one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProd_smul_of_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProd_smul_of_weight","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeSeminormalWeight.lean#L63-L76","doc":"**The ordered product of the JM elements acts by the product of the eigenvalues.**\n\nInduction on `n`.  The step needs the eigenvalue scalar to commute past `jmProd`, which it does\nbecause `Algebra R A` puts the image of `algebraMap` in the centre. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.IsJMWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.IsJMWeight","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeSeminormalWeight.lean#L56-L61","doc":"**A Jucys–Murphy weight vector**: every `Lₖ` with `k < n` acts on `v` by a scalar `cₖ`.\n\nThis is the seminormal form's defining property of a standard-tableau basis vector, stated without\nconstructing the basis. ","signatureChunk":0}]}